    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d763">

                <pb facs="0727" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg611"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.51/333.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 13, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am authorized by the President of Honduras to state that he will not again
                    submit to Congress the loan convention now pending in the United States Senate,
                    even if ratified by that body, considering the rejection by the Congress of
                    Honduras as final. He is however disposed to make a loan convention, since a
                    large loan is necessary but cannot be made except under such a guaranty.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">White.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
